   "t": "Понятно. Буду очень осторожной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Вот и молодец. За работу!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's break down this tense kitchen conversation sentence by sentence.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Почему на кухне так тихо?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why is the kitchen so quiet?' A question asking about the unusually tense atmosphere on the kitchen floor.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф идёт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef is coming.' A short subject and verb warning that the boss is approaching.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Опять злой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Angry again.' The adverb for 'again' paired with the short adjective describing the chef's foul mood.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Что случилось?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What happened?' The standard past-tense question for finding out what went wrong.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Опять футбол?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Football again?' Anya guesses the reason behind the chef's predictable anger.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Да, вчера играл Спартак.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, yesterday Spartak played.' Confirming that Barinov's beloved football team was on the pitch last night.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "И сколько он проиграл?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And how much did he lose?' Asking about the size of the chef's gambling bet.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Сто штук.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A hundred grand.' Slang for one hundred thousand rubles.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Ничего себе!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Unbelievable!' A very common Russian idiom expressing shock and astonishment.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Сто тысяч рублей?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A hundred thousand rubles?' Clarifying the enormous sum of money that was lost.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Да, ровно сто тысяч.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, exactly one hundred thousand.' The adverb emphasizes the precise and painful total.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Они всегда проигрывают перед сменой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They always lose before his shift.' Senya complains about the terrible timing of the football club's losses.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "И что теперь делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And what do we do now?' An essential phrase using the infinitive to ask what course of action to take.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Молчи и просто работай.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Stay silent and just work.' Two sharp imperatives advising head-down survival.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Не зли шефа сегодня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do not anger the chef today.' A negative imperative warning against provoking the temperamental head chef.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Понятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Understood.' A single word expressing comprehension and readiness.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Буду очень осторожной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will be very careful.' Using the future tense with the instrumental case for the adjective.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "За работу!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
